  "notes": "Giunta Muebles' Living N5, a show-room on the CASA FOA exhibition platform in Cordoba — an interior with no exterior of its own, so it is drawn as a cutaway set from the article's eighteen photographs: the room's walls lined in walnut (about 12.5 m by 5 m inside, guessed from the sofa, 1 m deep, and the coffee tables), the long art wall on the north with its band of dark green quartzite lit above the seating and five pale framed pictures over it, the olive L of sofa, the two olive armchairs under the tall green drapes at the west end, low black tables on a grey rug and an orange kilim, boards of oak on the floor. The south side is the photographed screen of horizontal timber slats with the indoor garden behind it (large-leaved plants in black pots in a strip 1.5 m deep, its charcoal back wall kept low so it reads). The west end is the double-height opening with its slatted shutter; the single-slope walnut ceiling is drawn only over that end, rising toward it, and the east end is left open and the rest of the ceiling off, so the room can be seen into from the four sides. Guessed: the room's real length and width, the heights (3.5 m, 5.5 at the garden end), the ceiling's slope, where the entrance is. The first model closed the box under a dark lid and put two trees at its door; both are gone."
